{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "reh11_grade_grid_blend",
  "spec": ["REH 4.5", "REH 11.5", "REH 10.3"],
  "description": "REH test 5 [quirk]. Tract (0, 0) with population 3000. School A (K-6, group 0, capacity 1500 -> units 3, n = 3, served 3000, grade 0.5): the grade grid gets 2 x 0 + (3 x 0.5) / 3 = 0.5. School B (group 2 = 0x1514, chunk 1000, capacity 3000 -> units 3) is funded at 50 % (a staff item of department 0x77, whose funding is 0.5): e1 = effCurve(50) x 0.01 = 0.5, e2 = 1.0, effective capacity 1500, served 3000, grade 0.5. Graded after A in the same pass, its n = 3 (coverage grid 2) multiplies the previous value: 2 x 0.5 + 0.5 = 1.5, clamped to 1.0.",
  "steps": [
    {"op": "residential_env", "groups": {"1": ["0x150F"]}, "props": {"1": {"0x8922041B": {"u32": 1500}, "0x691B42B3": {"f32": 10}}}, "lots": {"1": [32, 32]}},
    {"op": "residential_env", "groups": {"2": ["0x1514"]}, "props": {"2": {"0x8922041B": {"u32": 3000}, "0x691B42B3": {"f32": 10}}}, "lots": {"2": [32, 32]}},
